From e732d1392abde4ae49059c35344ed25aafefc806 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Eduardo=20Garc=C3=ADa-M=C3=A1dico=20Portabella?=
 <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 13:21:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 104/106] slimbus: no aplazar el sondeo si el dispositivo aun
 no tiene direccion

Anadido .laddr_optional a struct slim_driver. Con la bandera puesta,
slim_device_probe() deja el dispositivo ENLAZADO cuando
slim_get_logical_addr() falla, en vez de devolver -EPROBE_DEFER.

Por que hace falta: aplazar el sondeo deshace TODOS los recursos devm que
probe() acaba de registrar -en un codec, el componente ASoC que su tarjeta
de sonido esta esperando- y lo vuelve a deshacer en cada reintento. Un chip
que tarda segundos en enumerar (el WCN3990 solo responde despues de que
hci_uart cargue su firmware, y a veces nunca) dejaba a la tarjeta esperando
para siempre por un codec que se construia y se derribaba sin parar. El
driver lo rodeaba bloqueando 20 s dentro de su propio probe().

Y el aplazamiento no aportaba nada: slim_device_alloc_laddr() ya llama a
slim_device_update_status() cuando la direccion se asigna, incluido desde
slim_device_report_present() cuando el dispositivo aparece tarde, asi que
el driver se entera igual por su callback device_status().

Es opcion POR DRIVER: ningun otro cliente SLIMbus cambia de comportamiento.
Quien la ponga debe comprobar is_laddr_valid antes de hablar por el bus,
como ya hace wcn-bt-slim en cada acceso.

Verificado en surya, con el chip Bluetooth deliberadamente sin preparar:

  wcn-bt-slim 217:220:0:0: no logical address yet, staying bound
  wcn-bt-slim 217:220:1:0: no logical address yet, staying bound
  wcn-bt-slim 217:220:1:0: chip never showed up on the bus

y aun asi la tarjeta se registra CON su backend Bluetooth (el codec aparece
como componente en /sys/kernel/debug/asoc/, con sus mezcladores
SLIMBUS_7_TX), sin que haga falta el plazo del parche 0082. El insmod pasa
de bloquear 20 s por dispositivo a 3 s en total.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/slimbus/core.c  | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 include/linux/slimbus.h |  6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/slimbus/core.c b/drivers/slimbus/core.c
index ee6318e24..6d732b545 100644
--- a/drivers/slimbus/core.c
+++ b/drivers/slimbus/core.c
@@ -73,6 +73,23 @@ static int slim_device_probe(struct device *dev)
 	ret = slim_get_logical_addr(sbdev);
 	if (!ret) {
 		slim_device_update_status(sbdev, SLIM_DEVICE_STATUS_UP);
+	} else if (sbdrv->laddr_optional) {
+		/*
+		 * The device has not turned up on the bus yet. Deferring here
+		 * would undo everything probe() just registered - for a codec,
+		 * the ASoC component its sound card is waiting for - and undo
+		 * it again on every retry, so a chip that takes seconds to
+		 * enumerate leaves its consumers waiting forever on something
+		 * that keeps being torn down.
+		 *
+		 * Nothing is lost by staying bound: slim_device_alloc_laddr()
+		 * calls slim_device_update_status() whenever an address is
+		 * assigned, including from slim_device_report_present() when
+		 * the device finally announces itself, so the driver is still
+		 * told the moment it happens.
+		 */
+		dev_info(&sbdev->dev, "no logical address yet, staying bound\n");
+		ret = 0;
 	} else {
 		dev_err(&sbdev->dev, "Failed to get logical address\n");
 		ret = -EPROBE_DEFER;
diff --git a/include/linux/slimbus.h b/include/linux/slimbus.h
index 9e71fb549..282ec175e 100644
--- a/include/linux/slimbus.h
+++ b/include/linux/slimbus.h
@@ -80,6 +80,11 @@ struct slim_device {
  * @driver: SLIMbus device drivers should initialize name and owner field of
  *	    this structure
  * @id_table: List of SLIMbus devices supported by this driver
+ * @laddr_optional: Stay bound when the device has no logical address yet,
+ *	instead of having the probe deferred. For devices that take their time
+ *	turning up on the bus: the driver keeps everything it registered, and
+ *	@device_status tells it when the address finally arrives. Drivers that
+ *	set this must check &slim_device.is_laddr_valid before any bus traffic.
  */
 
 struct slim_driver {
@@ -90,6 +95,7 @@ struct slim_driver {
 				 enum slim_device_status s);
 	struct device_driver		driver;
 	const struct slim_device_id	*id_table;
+	bool				laddr_optional;
 };
 #define to_slim_driver(d) container_of_const(d, struct slim_driver, driver)
 
